[{:db/id 17592186192780 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-61609b84-fa99-5574-b117-b0c4a018b4cb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192782 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-24da091b-82da-56f5-873d-6d9cc1e779e2" "question-d4fcfc53-7279-50f5-90f1-bd8c9662d8f3" "question-8d538e48-6d40-5139-9e4a-4a2045c240b7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192781 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c109cc3b-b729-5d92-be15-5107dfc714ce" "question-784a3447-3ec5-5b3c-aa05-c4909c41863a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192505 :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it is not closed under scalar multiplication. For example, the vector ![](images/6d/6da77166b57246e3d4bb076af75c54a10350678986adfb6e31125e0ef614bacc.svg) belongs to $A,$ but the vector ![](images/9c/9cfd2972828a5c45bc58b434debbcf4a96c2cab14daa36a1e07fc37011682960.svg) does not lie in $A$ (because it does not satisfy $x^2=y$).\n\n- The set $B$ represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. If the origin belongs to this subset, we would have\n![](images/83/83ecb68263c21fca495034a2f1678dced07ddf9f5167c5a0a9c7703657530c47.svg)\nwhich gives us\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3-t=0 \\\\ -3+t=0 \\\\ -6+2t=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $t=3$ is the solution to the three equations. So, if we choose $t=3,$ then we find that $\\mathbf{0} \\in B.$ Therefore, $B$ is a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-61609b84-fa99-5574-b117-b0c4a018b4cb" :question/id #uuid "61609b84-fa99-5574-b117-b0c4a018b4cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-110456" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5ac6c0c6dc06d6e9b3970f2d6e5c5ce01a56c781143999d744a9b3914c37a49d.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents a set that does not contain the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$ without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fe451965-9c74-57be-8dbe-36a5fd0d6066"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fe451965-9c74-57be-8dbe-36a5fd0d6066" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe451965-9c74-57be-8dbe-36a5fd0d6066" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-454f98bf-3629-5a58-9552-960add2da6f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b4bc555d-4c0a-5189-8ed7-e64a95c92fbe" "answer-0fbb2cff-4624-5923-8685-e5a548d8977d" "answer-f5dd10dc-46c8-5e11-9117-cbcf71fba3aa" "answer-7a1b4867-eb6a-5521-bcad-61fa3407334a" "answer-454f98bf-3629-5a58-9552-960add2da6f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4bc555d-4c0a-5189-8ed7-e64a95c92fbe" :answer/id #uuid "b4bc555d-4c0a-5189-8ed7-e64a95c92fbe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fbb2cff-4624-5923-8685-e5a548d8977d" :answer/id #uuid "0fbb2cff-4624-5923-8685-e5a548d8977d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5dd10dc-46c8-5e11-9117-cbcf71fba3aa" :answer/id #uuid "f5dd10dc-46c8-5e11-9117-cbcf71fba3aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a1b4867-eb6a-5521-bcad-61fa3407334a" :answer/id #uuid "7a1b4867-eb6a-5521-bcad-61fa3407334a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-454f98bf-3629-5a58-9552-960add2da6f7" :answer/id #uuid "454f98bf-3629-5a58-9552-960add2da6f7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-24da091b-82da-56f5-873d-6d9cc1e779e2" :question/id #uuid "24da091b-82da-56f5-873d-6d9cc1e779e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-158072" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8f3c0e576491c4fd3897e30931ca7ed86d03c557ed37de86a3bcdc748f2263ea.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}$ or ${R}^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ clearly lies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ clearly lies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III represents a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fba70771-0732-5f16-8aad-3cbb450dac29"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fba70771-0732-5f16-8aad-3cbb450dac29" :answer-field/id #uuid "fba70771-0732-5f16-8aad-3cbb450dac29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8dcc7e06-175d-5d1b-a601-c0adc25aeb03" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0767be10-b80e-5b7a-9933-3ba3fb4c44e8" "answer-a7a01f3a-a811-5cfd-9def-5a3a838e631f" "answer-5d6b65ab-8807-5d54-926e-ee314453bf97" "answer-c55dee9a-9cbf-579c-a16e-bc04fcd4e0d9" "answer-8dcc7e06-175d-5d1b-a601-c0adc25aeb03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0767be10-b80e-5b7a-9933-3ba3fb4c44e8" :answer/id #uuid "0767be10-b80e-5b7a-9933-3ba3fb4c44e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7a01f3a-a811-5cfd-9def-5a3a838e631f" :answer/id #uuid "a7a01f3a-a811-5cfd-9def-5a3a838e631f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d6b65ab-8807-5d54-926e-ee314453bf97" :answer/id #uuid "5d6b65ab-8807-5d54-926e-ee314453bf97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c55dee9a-9cbf-579c-a16e-bc04fcd4e0d9" :answer/id #uuid "c55dee9a-9cbf-579c-a16e-bc04fcd4e0d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8dcc7e06-175d-5d1b-a601-c0adc25aeb03" :answer/id #uuid "8dcc7e06-175d-5d1b-a601-c0adc25aeb03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d4fcfc53-7279-50f5-90f1-bd8c9662d8f3" :question/id #uuid "d4fcfc53-7279-50f5-90f1-bd8c9662d8f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-110599" :question/problem "![](images/c3/c36c34462f2ba7f129ba3370d4e67c5ac450b4188be629a256caf7807d4cb2d6.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}$ or ${R}^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$  clearly lies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. There are vectors  $a=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$  in the subset for which ${a}_{1}>0$ and ${a}_{2}>0.$   But then\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}-{a}_{1} \\\\ -{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III is a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-913f9620-3143-5eb0-bde3-3581baeee85f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-913f9620-3143-5eb0-bde3-3581baeee85f" :answer-field/id #uuid "913f9620-3143-5eb0-bde3-3581baeee85f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c12258e1-34ad-53a0-a3d9-9235459976ea" :answer-field/choices ["answer-abdf6d49-ea74-5c07-a09b-16cb093c715a" "answer-b5069048-3871-5ac2-9c3f-95c0913fd49a" "answer-fc8e878f-5e6c-568c-8370-d1b742bed8da" "answer-5caf0a31-9e0c-5a1c-ad65-9b44460cbe33" "answer-c12258e1-34ad-53a0-a3d9-9235459976ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abdf6d49-ea74-5c07-a09b-16cb093c715a" :answer/id #uuid "abdf6d49-ea74-5c07-a09b-16cb093c715a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5069048-3871-5ac2-9c3f-95c0913fd49a" :answer/id #uuid "b5069048-3871-5ac2-9c3f-95c0913fd49a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc8e878f-5e6c-568c-8370-d1b742bed8da" :answer/id #uuid "fc8e878f-5e6c-568c-8370-d1b742bed8da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5caf0a31-9e0c-5a1c-ad65-9b44460cbe33" :answer/id #uuid "5caf0a31-9e0c-5a1c-ad65-9b44460cbe33" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c12258e1-34ad-53a0-a3d9-9235459976ea" :answer/id #uuid "c12258e1-34ad-53a0-a3d9-9235459976ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8d538e48-6d40-5139-9e4a-4a2045c240b7" :question/id #uuid "8d538e48-6d40-5139-9e4a-4a2045c240b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-158073" :question/problem "![](images/f6/f6695911ed29ccf88240660e45ce6527c0a10e3cf8d6a299ac9eef2be3ff53cb.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I represents a plane that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- Diagram II represents a line that does not pass through the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so the line in Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-32d5a140-6abb-5e9f-bd19-77d2f7c496f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-32d5a140-6abb-5e9f-bd19-77d2f7c496f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "32d5a140-6abb-5e9f-bd19-77d2f7c496f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3785fa9c-48ca-585d-98ad-b79c1eb2860b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3785fa9c-48ca-585d-98ad-b79c1eb2860b" "answer-963d4f9f-58da-588d-9b63-7579100345e3" "answer-87caa511-9031-5f67-b7b1-5bebef022d31" "answer-0d497d71-015c-5091-8ed9-1e92e99927de" "answer-ae8b5893-8336-52d6-9374-ab8aa55e5655"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3785fa9c-48ca-585d-98ad-b79c1eb2860b" :answer/id #uuid "3785fa9c-48ca-585d-98ad-b79c1eb2860b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-963d4f9f-58da-588d-9b63-7579100345e3" :answer/id #uuid "963d4f9f-58da-588d-9b63-7579100345e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87caa511-9031-5f67-b7b1-5bebef022d31" :answer/id #uuid "87caa511-9031-5f67-b7b1-5bebef022d31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d497d71-015c-5091-8ed9-1e92e99927de" :answer/id #uuid "0d497d71-015c-5091-8ed9-1e92e99927de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae8b5893-8336-52d6-9374-ab8aa55e5655" :answer/id #uuid "ae8b5893-8336-52d6-9374-ab8aa55e5655" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c109cc3b-b729-5d92-be15-5107dfc714ce" :question/id #uuid "c109cc3b-b729-5d92-be15-5107dfc714ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-110759" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nI. $A=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x-y+z=0\\}$\n\nII. $B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=0\\}$\n\nIII. $C=\\{⟨0,0,1⟩\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x-y+z=0$ since $0-0+0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $A.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. This subset has only one element, the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩,$ which is a special (trivial) subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace. This subset has only one element, the vector $⟨0,0,1⟩,$ so it does not contain the zero vector.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1275155b-aac2-554a-8a20-c373814f14d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1275155b-aac2-554a-8a20-c373814f14d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "1275155b-aac2-554a-8a20-c373814f14d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-554e7d19-0e14-5830-b0fd-7d5b3f83ee7f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-554e7d19-0e14-5830-b0fd-7d5b3f83ee7f" "answer-bcb5e878-1dd3-5cc3-a04a-226eaf163c85" "answer-b5f99f31-23ce-57b2-a47b-0e3dfda5c91a" "answer-a8ae60eb-fe33-51ae-8844-4f984b797389" "answer-fe20b5d4-90f9-54c8-9931-1ec170ceeb0e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-554e7d19-0e14-5830-b0fd-7d5b3f83ee7f" :answer/id #uuid "554e7d19-0e14-5830-b0fd-7d5b3f83ee7f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcb5e878-1dd3-5cc3-a04a-226eaf163c85" :answer/id #uuid "bcb5e878-1dd3-5cc3-a04a-226eaf163c85" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5f99f31-23ce-57b2-a47b-0e3dfda5c91a" :answer/id #uuid "b5f99f31-23ce-57b2-a47b-0e3dfda5c91a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8ae60eb-fe33-51ae-8844-4f984b797389" :answer/id #uuid "a8ae60eb-fe33-51ae-8844-4f984b797389" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe20b5d4-90f9-54c8-9931-1ec170ceeb0e" :answer/id #uuid "fe20b5d4-90f9-54c8-9931-1ec170ceeb0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-784a3447-3ec5-5b3c-aa05-c4909c41863a" :question/id #uuid "784a3447-3ec5-5b3c-aa05-c4909c41863a" :question/math-academy-id "q-110763" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nI. $A=\\{⟨1+t,t-1⟩\\,:\\,t\\in R\\}$\n\nII. $B=\\{⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:xy=0\\}$\n\nIII. $C=\\{⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x=0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. If the origin belongs to this subset, we would have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1+t \\\\ t-1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives us\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}t+1=0 \\\\ t-1=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the system has no solution. So, $0$ is not in $A.$\n\n- The set $B$ is not a subspace. Indeed, both $a=⟨1,0⟩$ and $b=⟨0,1⟩$ belong to $B$ but \n\n$$\na+b=⟨1,0⟩+⟨0,1⟩=⟨1,1⟩\n$$\n\n \ndoes not satisfy the condition $xy=0$ since $1\\cdot 1\\ne 0.$\n\n- The set $C$ is a subspace. It represents a line (the $y$-axis), and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x=0$ since $0=0.$ So, $0$ lies in $C.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9c8d6b0d-91c0-5042-9591-44d5f308c893"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c8d6b0d-91c0-5042-9591-44d5f308c893" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c8d6b0d-91c0-5042-9591-44d5f308c893" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8cf25f88-fff3-55ab-bc62-d7f0f4626567" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cdb8646c-5884-5c39-bedb-ba79ac30411d" "answer-fea4f0b9-381b-5720-8ec6-11a187e7c372" "answer-39a386ac-92e4-5de2-b25a-a233d3727e10" "answer-ac955eaa-6ad8-5245-bdc3-f9b1b5a756a1" "answer-8cf25f88-fff3-55ab-bc62-d7f0f4626567"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdb8646c-5884-5c39-bedb-ba79ac30411d" :answer/id #uuid "cdb8646c-5884-5c39-bedb-ba79ac30411d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fea4f0b9-381b-5720-8ec6-11a187e7c372" :answer/id #uuid "fea4f0b9-381b-5720-8ec6-11a187e7c372" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39a386ac-92e4-5de2-b25a-a233d3727e10" :answer/id #uuid "39a386ac-92e4-5de2-b25a-a233d3727e10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac955eaa-6ad8-5245-bdc3-f9b1b5a756a1" :answer/id #uuid "ac955eaa-6ad8-5245-bdc3-f9b1b5a756a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cf25f88-fff3-55ab-bc62-d7f0f4626567" :answer/id #uuid "8cf25f88-fff3-55ab-bc62-d7f0f4626567" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317380 :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nI. $A=\\{⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 0\\}$\n\nII. $B=\\{⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x=2y\\}$\n\nIII. $C=\\{⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x-y=0\\}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247159 :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nI. $A=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x-4y=1\\}$\n\nII. $B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x=-2y\\}$\n\nIII. $C=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0\\}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186342191 :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nI. $A=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}<\\frac{1}{2}\\}$\n\nII. $B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:5x-y-z=0\\}$\n\nIII. $C=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:5-x-z=0\\}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
